:Situation_T1_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "A government official uses 'a few bad apples' to describe police misconduct as the fault of isolated individuals, explicitly rejecting a systemic explanation."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://abcnews.com/US/bad-apples-phrase-describing-rotten-police-officers-meaning/story?id=71201096> .

:Situation_T2_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "An academic article names the 'bad apples' phrase as a narrative and criticises it for hiding systemic racism in policing."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://theconversation.com/police-violence-in-the-united-states-what-lies-behind-the-bad-apples-narrative-139931> .

:Situation_T3_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "A cybersecurity company uses the proverb to present unprotected employees as the point where attackers break into a business, to sell protection for every employee."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.upfort.com/blog-articles/no-more-weakest-links-why-every-employee-needs-cybersecurity-protection> .

:Situation_T4_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "An HR blog uses the proverb to praise quiet, introverted employees as having hidden value that managers overlook."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.hrzone.com/talent/development/blog-still-waters-run-deep-never-underestimate-an-introvert> .

:Situation_T5_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "Forum users disagree on whether the proverb praises quiet people or warns against them; one user counts 5 negative, 2 positive and 3 unclear uses in a corpus."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://forum.wordreference.com/threads/still-water-runs-deep.448648/> .

:Situation_T6_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "An opinion piece uses the proverb in its title as a warning to powerful politicians that their actions will come back to them."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gazetatema.net/web/2015/03/03/historia-e-te-forteve-ne-politike-ose-cfare-te-mbjellesh-do-korresh> .

:Situation_T6_2 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "The Prime Minister uses the sow/reap image to promise that reforms 'sown' today will bring success in 2017."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gazetatema.net/web/2015/03/03/historia-e-te-forteve-ne-politike-ose-cfare-te-mbjellesh-do-korresh> .

:Situation_T7_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "A politician posts the proverb on Instagram during the European migration crisis, warning that harsh or careless policies will come back as larger problems."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://agenziastampaitalia.it/politica/politica-nazionale/74957-migranti-casini-avviso-ai-naviganti-chi-semina-vento-raccoglie-tempesta> .

:Situation_T8_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "A newspaper editorial applies the proverb to politicians who distribute improper favours and so impoverish the population."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://qds.it/chi-semina-vento-raccoglie-tempesta/> .

:Situation_T8_2 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "The same editorial applies the proverb to citizens who repeat political slogans instead of thinking, and 'reap' high abstention and a weak democracy."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://qds.it/chi-semina-vento-raccoglie-tempesta/> .

:Situation_T9_1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        proto:SituationOfUse ;
    rdfs:label "A personal blog retells the folk tale and explains that the proverb is said of anyone who, out of friendship, does something that ends up harming the other person."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://nahidkhirolahi.blogfa.com/post/199> .

